5. Linux kernel patches
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Kernel patches shipped under the platform submodule apply to Linux 4.9.57 as
distributed in the OCTEON SDK, which is GPL-2.0. The unmodified upstream code
remains under its own licence; the hunks FFN adds are FFN's own work under
GPL-2.0-or-later. Each patch carries a header naming the upstream file it
applies to.


-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
6. What is deliberately absent
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

No vendor firmware, kernel image, kernel module, bootloader, root filesystem,
FPGA bitstream, configuration file, or source code is redistributed by this
project, in this repository or any other. Where vendor firmware is required to
bring a board up, it is used in place on the appliance the operator already
owns.

That is enforced, not merely promised: `ffn_vendor.py` has a `check-clean` mode
whose job is to prove no vendor-supplied content has entered a build.
